# Binary fixture files must never go through git's line-ending
# normalization. Without this, a clone with core.autocrlf enabled (the
# default on Windows/Git for Windows) silently rewrites any LF byte that
# looks like a text line ending inside these files, corrupting them -
# NetCDF4/HDF5 files fail to open afterward with a generic
# "NetCDF: HDF error" (the HDF5 superblock no longer parses), not a more
# obviously binary-corruption-shaped error.
*.nc binary
*.tif binary
*.tiff binary

# WPS_GEOG-format geogrid tile data files (numeric NNNNN-NNNNN.NNNNN-NNNNN
# names, e.g. tests/fixtures/geotiff_convert/wps_soiltemp_1deg/*) are raw
# binary tile data, not text, despite having no distinguishing extension.
[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9].[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9] binary
